WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.972
Hey, this is Anton from the Adobe Premiere

00:00:02.972 --> 00:00:05.040
team and I'm excited to show you our new

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:08.172
generative media tool in Premiere. Let's jump right

00:00:08.172 --> 00:00:11.120
into a real edit. This commercial is almost done

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:13.534
but still has a few gaps. Let me show you how

00:00:13.534 --> 00:00:15.840
to fill them without ever leaving the edit.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:18.955
With the new generative media tool you can generate

00:00:18.955 --> 00:00:21.360
videos and sound effects right in your timeline.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.674
First up is this visual gap.

00:00:23.674 --> 00:00:25.887
The edit is missing an area shot that

00:00:25.887 --> 00:00:27.920
the crew couldn't get on location.

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.127
Here's how it works. Pick the tool then

00:00:30.127 --> 00:00:32.560
click and drag to create a range selection.

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:35.234
That range can be on any video track,

00:00:35.234 --> 00:00:37.063
audio track or both if the model

00:00:37.063 --> 00:00:38.720
supports it. It works similar

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:41.710
to a clip. You can trim it, move it and it'll snap

00:00:41.710 --> 00:00:44.640
into place. You can also simply double click on a

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:47.272
gap in the timeline. The new generative taskbar

00:00:47.272 --> 00:00:49.680
is your hub for everything that comes next.

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:52.894
Firstly, you can choose between a variety of

00:00:52.894 --> 00:00:55.760
Adobe Firefly and partner models like Google Vio,

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:58.234
Kling or Luma. I'll use Vio for this

00:00:58.234 --> 00:01:00.640
shot and already prepared a prompt.

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:03.015
A prompt alone won't match my project though.

00:01:03.015 --> 00:01:04.757
To get a production ready output,

00:01:04.757 --> 00:01:05.760
the model needs the

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:07.407
visual context of my project.

00:01:07.407 --> 00:01:09.566
In Premiere, I can now natively sample

00:01:09.566 --> 00:01:11.440
reference frames straight from my

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:14.342
own footage. You can pick the frames left and right

00:01:14.342 --> 00:01:16.960
to the selected range, sample any frame in the

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:18.988
project or use one from your device.

00:01:18.988 --> 00:01:20.847
We are bringing the models to the

00:01:20.847 --> 00:01:22.480
footage instead of taking the

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:24.956
footage to the model. So there is no context

00:01:24.956 --> 00:01:27.600
switching and no exporting. The feature detects

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:30.330
your sequence specs like aspect ratio and resolution

00:01:30.330 --> 00:01:32.640
and auto matches them to the model's nearest

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:34.848
available option. For this drone shot,

00:01:34.848 --> 00:01:36.591
the only thing I need to do is

00:01:36.591 --> 00:01:38.160
find a good frame like this

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:41.086
one and sample it with one click using the built-in

00:01:41.086 --> 00:01:43.840
eyedropper. If you ever need to go back and fine

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:46.280
tune or double check the reference you used,

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:47.888
simply click the new AI badge

00:01:47.888 --> 00:01:49.440
and get back to the taskbar.

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:52.717
For the intro, I also want a desert ambient sound

00:01:52.717 --> 00:01:54.960
effect, but I don't have one in my library.

00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:58.396
Same idea, I draw a range on my audio track and

00:01:58.396 --> 00:02:01.200
describe the sound I want. I can even use my voice

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:03.154
to guide the timing and intensity

00:02:03.154 --> 00:02:05.166
so it lands exactly how I need it.

00:02:05.166 --> 00:02:07.120
Let's add a few final tweaks like

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:08.361
these smooth audio fades,

00:02:08.361 --> 00:02:10.000
then give it a look and a listen.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:16.058
Everything you just saw happened all without ever

00:02:16.058 --> 00:02:22.240
leaving the edit. This is the new generative media

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:24.772
tool in Premiere, the first step of AI generation

00:02:24.772 --> 00:02:27.200
that lives where your video project already is.

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:29.171
Thanks for watching,

00:02:29.171 --> 00:02:32.720
I can't wait to see what you create.
